From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 09:40:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733: Give the IOMMUs the video engine
 port gates

A master's register block in the IOMMU does not answer while the
master's port on the MBUS matrix is gated, and the access stalls the
bus. The IOMMU driver takes a reference on the port gate of a master,
given as a "masterN" clock, for as long as the master translates. The
A733 clock driver marks these gates CLK_IS_CRITICAL, so they stay
enabled and the reference does not change their state.

Name the port gates of the video engine's masters. The decoder's two
masters, 0 and 1 of the second IOMMU, share the decoder's port gate,
bit 14 of MBUS_MAT_CLK_GATING_REG. The encoder's master, 3 of the first
IOMMU, has the encoder's, bit 12 (manual section 4.1.6.83; the master
numbers are in chapter 10).

Seen on the Radxa Cubie A7S: with the port gates of the video engine
cleared, the first unmap through its masters stalls the bus until the
watchdog resets the SoC. With only the port gates set, and the engine's
resets, bus gates and clocks off, the unmaps complete.

Nothing changes until a node lists the IOMMU in "iommus": the driver
enables a master clock only for a master with a user. The other masters
have no consumer yet and no port gate named.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on one board; the IOMMUs bound and
appear as consumers of the port gates of the video engine's decoder and
encoder masters, and the gates read enabled in MBUS_MAT_CLK_GATING_REG.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi | 13 +++++++++----
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
index e0a063bd606e..0351369ef174 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
@@ -813,8 +813,10 @@ iommu0: iommu@3900000 {
 			clocks = <&ccu CLK_MBUS_IOMMU0_SYS>,
 				 <&ccu CLK_APB_IOMMU0_SYS>,
 				 <&ccu CLK_AHB_IOMMU0_SYS>,
-				 <&ccu CLK_MBUS_IOMMU0>;
-			clock-names = "mclk", "pclk", "hclk", "mbus";
+				 <&ccu CLK_MBUS_IOMMU0>,
+				 <&ccu CLK_MBUS_VE_ENC0_GATE>;
+			clock-names = "mclk", "pclk", "hclk", "mbus",
+				      "master3";
 			resets = <&ccu RST_BUS_IOMMU0_SYS>;
 			#iommu-cells = <1>;
 		};
@@ -826,8 +828,11 @@ iommu1: iommu@3910000 {
 			clocks = <&ccu CLK_MBUS_IOMMU1_SYS>,
 				 <&ccu CLK_APB_IOMMU1_SYS>,
 				 <&ccu CLK_AHB_IOMMU1_SYS>,
-				 <&ccu CLK_MBUS_IOMMU1>;
-			clock-names = "mclk", "pclk", "hclk", "mbus";
+				 <&ccu CLK_MBUS_IOMMU1>,
+				 <&ccu CLK_MBUS_VE_DEC0_GATE>,
+				 <&ccu CLK_MBUS_VE_DEC0_GATE>;
+			clock-names = "mclk", "pclk", "hclk", "mbus",
+				      "master0", "master1";
 			resets = <&ccu RST_BUS_IOMMU1_SYS>;
 			#iommu-cells = <1>;
 		};
